# Project Management List
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: Project Management — a column on a Board; its order among sibling Lists is
# freely dragged by a Member, not computed from any field. Same for Card below.
# Case 19 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# References: pm-board.menata, pm-card.menata
#
# THE NEW FINDING THIS CASE EXISTS TO SURFACE: CAP-V04 (default_sort) is a
# *declarative* sort rule in metadata — e.g. "order by Sequence ascending." Position
# here is different: a Member drags a List or Card to a new spot, and the *data
# itself* changes to reflect an arbitrary, user-chosen order with no formula behind
# it. No capability names user-editable manual ordering.

List

Fields

- Board : Board
- Name : Text
- Position : Number

Constraints

- Board is required.
- Name is required.

Permissions

Member

- Reorder

Views

- Board Lists : List
